P-Test (Hypothesis Testing) - Quick Notes
H₀ and H₁ are mutually exclusive: If one is true, the other is false.
Focuses on a single test statistic: A value that summarizes the sample data.
Calculate the test statistic: (e.g., Z, t, χ², F) using sample data.
Apply the decision rule:
If p-value ≤ α → Reject H₀
If p-value > α → Fail to reject H₀
Steps
State H₀ and H₁
Calculate test statistic
Find p-value/critical value
Apply decision rule
Draw conclusion

